```--------------------To generate the Assert statements, we would need a tool to parse the code and match the comments that start with "@@@" to the corresponding code snippets. Here is a simple Python script that uses regular expressions to accomplish this:

```python
import re

code = """
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_CountContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);


            int New_Ret = arrList.Count;


            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_ret", New_Ret);


	    // @@@ count value of array is either 0 or greater than or equal to one 
        }
    }
}
"""

# Regular expression to find comments starting with "@@@"
comments = re.findall(r'// @@@ (.*)', code)

print(comments)
```

